{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/969915-social-combat-maneuvering","id":969915,"title":"Social Combat/Maneuvering","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-15T08:06:18-07:00","id":969915,"title":"Social Combat/Maneuvering","content":"I need a Refresher on handling social combat between two players or a player and NPC. I've been handling it by subtracting the opposition's composure from the aggressor dice pool and rolling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:16:43-07:00","id":970210,"title":"","content":"That's basically how Forcing Doors works, except with remaining Doors instead of Composure. <br /> You can resolve simple social interactions like any other roll, sometimes Contested sometimes not. Not everything has to be done trough social maneuvering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:24:16-07:00","id":970222,"title":"","content":"I was just worried about being too easy or too hard with the situations. Didn't want it be too easy to persuade or be persuaded","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:29:55-07:00","id":970230,"title":"","content":"Get your hands on the God-Machine rules appendix update, you got Social Maneuvering there, and it's free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:01:54-07:00","id":970253,"title":"","content":"So, characters have a number of Doors equal to the lower of their Resolve or Composure, which may be increased or decreased depending on what the actor is asking of them - for example, if complying would cause the character to suffer a Breaking Point you add a Door, or if it would cause them to fulfill an Aspiration you remove a Door. In order to get someone to do what you want, you must open all of their Doors. You can open Doors in one of two ways: Social Maneuvering, or Forcing Doors. <br /> <br /> In Social Maneuvering, each successful roll opens one Door (regardless of the number of successes rolled). You can only roll at certain intervals, determined by the subject's Impression of the actor, which typically starts at Neutral (1 roll per week), and can be increased with effort to appease the subject, requiring no roll to get to Good (1 roll per day), or a rolled action of some sort to get to Excellent (1 roll per hour). A Perfect Impression (1 roll per turn) can only be achieved via Soft Leverage - gifts, bribes, etc. Soft Leverage automatically increases a subject's Impression of the actor by one step if the subject accepts the offer. Upsetting the subject can set the Impression to Hostile (no rolls possible until the Impression improves to Neutral or better).<br /> <br /> Forcing Doors represents pressuring the subject into an immediate decision. It condenses the whole process into a single pass/fail dice roll, with the subject's Doors acting as a penalty to the actor's dice pool. On a success, the subject complies; on a failure, the subject does not comply, and the actor can not engage in further Social Maneuvering with the subject. Personally, I slightly house rule this to setting the Impression to Hostile, so the possibility of getting back into the subject's good graces remains open, but requires effort. Additionally, Forcing Doors can benefit from Hard Leverage - threats, blackmail, etc. Hard Leverage acts as a bonus to the actor's dice pool.<br /> <br /> If the subject is a Player Character and they have all of their Doors opened, they can opt not to comply with the actor's request, but instead offer an alternative that still benefits the actor, at the cost of taking a Condition, usually chosen by the actor, but subject to Storyteller discretion. If the do choose to comply, they gain a Beat.<br /> <br /> Of course, the above system isn't the only way to resolve Social actions at the table. You can always use standard Instant or Extended actions, or adapt the Combat or Chase rules to Social situations if you like. Personally, I love the Social Maneuvering and Forcing Doors system and use it for all Social actions, but it's far from the only way to resolve such actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-15-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}